# Session Abstraction Rule

## Core Requirements
- Single session wrapper for all auth logic
- Isolate session access to one service
- No raw session checks in components

## Implementation
- Primary Auth Context: [src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx](mdc:src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx)
- Supabase Client: [src/integrations/supabase/client.ts](mdc:src/integrations/supabase/client.ts)
- Session Refresh: [src/utils/reconnectHandler.ts](mdc:src/utils/reconnectHandler.ts)

## Session Management Guidelines
1. Use AuthContext for session state
2. Handle token refresh automatically
3. Implement proper session cleanup
4. Manage session persistence

## Security Rules
- Never store sensitive session data in localStorage
- Implement proper session timeout
- Handle session expiry gracefully
- Use secure session cookies
- Implement proper CSRF protection

## Usage Examples
```typescript
// Correct usage
const { session, user } = useAuth();

// Incorrect - don't access session directly
const session = supabase.auth.session();
```

